- [Gary] Hey Amanda.

00:05:34.355 --> 00:05:37.024
- My question is, roughly what percentage

00:05:37.024 --> 00:05:39.818
of your business decisions
are based on a gut feeling

00:05:39.818 --> 00:05:42.029
versus being backed by actual data?

00:05:43.405 --> 00:05:45.449
- Oh, that's a very good question.

00:05:45.449 --> 00:05:46.867
(laughter)

00:05:48.369 --> 00:05:50.746
I think all of my strategy

00:05:51.705 --> 00:05:53.499
is completely intuition,

00:05:53.499 --> 00:05:56.877
because if you look at my 20 year career,

00:05:56.877 --> 00:06:00.339
most of it has been guessing,

00:06:00.339 --> 00:06:03.717
I'd like to think projecting
where the market's gonna go.

00:06:03.717 --> 00:06:08.013
And there was no data on what
e-commerce would do in 1996,

00:06:08.013 --> 00:06:10.808
there was no data on email
marketing when you're one of

00:06:10.808 --> 00:06:13.268
the first hundred people
that's doing email marketing.

00:06:13.268 --> 00:06:16.355
There was no data on the ROI of Twitter

00:06:16.355 --> 00:06:18.232
four or five months after Twitter came out

00:06:18.232 --> 00:06:19.441
and you're starting to
use it for marketing.

00:06:19.441 --> 00:06:21.944
There was no data on what
a YouTube show less than

00:06:21.944 --> 00:06:25.114
a year after YouTube came out
was going to bring in value.

00:06:25.114 --> 00:06:27.699
There was no data on
what Instagram was gonna

00:06:27.699 --> 00:06:29.910
bring us in value when
AJ sold Brisk Iced Tea

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:33.664
an Instagram campaign 13 days
after Instagram had come out.

00:06:33.664 --> 00:06:36.834
There was no data around what
Vine celebrities would mean

00:06:36.834 --> 00:06:40.337
when we started a Vine agency
110 days after Vine came out.

00:06:40.337 --> 00:06:43.966
So, from a strategy
standpoint, I mean truly

00:06:43.966 --> 00:06:46.218
I believe that I get
the accolades and have

00:06:46.218 --> 00:06:48.262
the luxury of doing a show that people

00:06:48.262 --> 00:06:50.848
actually watch, completely on intuition,

00:06:50.848 --> 00:06:53.058
because that’s what I have
that other people don’t have.

00:06:53.058 --> 00:06:54.768
It’s no different than
being great at basketball

00:06:54.768 --> 00:06:57.229
or being attractive or
all the other good things

00:06:57.229 --> 00:06:59.523
that can happen in life,
it's just there, right?

00:06:59.523 --> 00:07:01.024
It was just always there.

00:07:01.024 --> 00:07:03.527
And so that's my X factor.

00:07:03.527 --> 00:07:06.405
Now, I think that is equally then

00:07:06.405 --> 00:07:10.951
50% quantified against data, right?

00:07:10.951 --> 00:07:15.330
So I make these predictions,
but then to run an actual

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:18.250
business, this is where my
practicality gets underestimated.

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.586
You know, this company grew very quickly,

00:07:20.586 --> 00:07:23.088
you don’t do that if you
can’t make payroll, right?

00:07:23.088 --> 00:07:24.840
There's a lot of practicality
(laughter)

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:27.342
that goes into running a business.

00:07:27.342 --> 00:07:29.928
And so, for me I've always thought I was

00:07:29.928 --> 00:07:34.141
a super 50/50 guy,
obviously my personality

00:07:34.141 --> 00:07:38.437
and communication style
gets most people’s attention

00:07:38.437 --> 00:07:41.023
and they bucket me into
that kind of place,

00:07:41.023 --> 00:07:43.734
but I take enormous pride
out of the fact that,

00:07:43.734 --> 00:07:46.445
for the first ten years
of my professional career,

00:07:46.445 --> 00:07:48.906
I didn't say a single word
to anybody about anything

00:07:48.906 --> 00:07:51.575
and all I did was execute, and
I'll be very honest with you,

00:07:51.575 --> 00:07:54.244
it's been extremely gratifying to me

00:07:54.244 --> 00:07:57.539
to shut up all the people that thought,

00:07:57.539 --> 00:07:58.957
when I was building VaynerMedia that,

00:07:58.957 --> 00:08:00.834
"Mister Lot of Twitter Followers,"

00:08:00.834 --> 00:08:02.878
like there was a
substantial amount of buzz

00:08:02.878 --> 00:08:04.880
when I started VaynerMedia of like, "Oh,

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:07.925
"this social media guru thinks
he can build an agency."

00:08:07.925 --> 00:08:09.426
And now building one of the biggest

00:08:09.426 --> 00:08:11.803
and fastest growing agencies of all time

00:08:11.803 --> 00:08:15.641
and sticking that directly in
their throat feels tremendous.

00:08:15.641 --> 00:08:18.352
